WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.830
A jester with a small drum
wanders between two great houses.

2
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.850
At the duke's, he sings.

3
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.940
Above the duke's head, a swirling opal.

4
00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.050
At the countess's, he jokes.

5
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.100
She wears a mourning veil.

6
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.920
He's a paid jester.

7
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:19.130
Yet the duke and the countess
both keep listening to him.

8
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:23.120
His motto: "Better a witty
fool than a foolish wit."

9
00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:27.320
So how can the fool be the
wisest person in the play?

10
00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.060
In this mission, you'll find
out what an allowed fool was.

11
00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:33.850
You'll watch him joke with
Olivia about her mourning,

12
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.110
line by line.

13
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.560
And you'll listen to his songs.

14
00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:42.190
Your mission: explain how the fool
can be the wisest person in the play.
